{"doc":"Statistics of the Python route/circuits.py build_jobs(seed=31, 2000, max_n=30, scale=S) for S = 0.5 (the campaign) and 1.0. A job is kept when its circuit fits (m <= topology n; the Python generator skips others, 'jobs_kept' counts survivors). Per job: n = circuit qubits; ops = number of ops; twoq_frac = (#ops with b >= 0) / ops (cx, cz, swap and the 2-qubit u2 count; u1, measure, barrier do not); depth = ASAP layering where an op occupies qubit a and, when b >= 0, qubit b (every op is one layer step on each qubit it touches); n_over_topology_n = n / (number of qubits of the topology the job targets). Categorical tables: family_counts (circuit family), topology_counts (25 training topologies by name), topology_family_counts. Continuous features are given as an ECDF knot set: x = sorted distinct values of the smallest sample x_k with ECDF(x_k) >= k/32 (k = 1..31), F = the reference ECDF evaluated at that x (ties included). Two-sample KS statistic of a Mojo sample against the reference: D = max over knots of |F_mojo(x) - F|, to be compared with the critical value c * sqrt(1/n_ref + 1/n_mojo) plus a 1/32 knot-spacing allowance (c = 2.28 for ~4 sigma). n_hist is the exact histogram of n per circuit family.","scales":[{"scale":0.5,"seed":31,"jobs_requested":2000,"jobs_kept":2000,"max_n":30,"family_counts":{"rand2q":341,"qv":325,"qft":338,"trotter":331,"qaoa":326,"sparse":339},"topology_counts":{"grid3x3":82,"grid4x4":88,"grid5x5":71,"grid6x6":71,"grid3x5":89,"heavy_hex19":85,"heavy_hex57":96,"diag18":71,"diag25":63,"oct16":76,"oct32":81,"line8":88,"line12":85,"line20":78,"ring8":80,"ring14":92,"ring20":92,"tree15":67,"tree31":78,"torus16":76,"torus25":71,"atom_r2_16":73,"atom_r2_25":88,"ionring12":72,"ionring16":87},"topology_family_counts":{"diag_grid":134,"grid":401,"heavy_hex":181,"ion_ring":159,"line":251,"neutral_atom":161,"octagonal":157,"ring":264,"torus":147,"tree":145},"all":{"n":{"n":2000,"mean":12.7485,"x":[4.0,5.0,6.0,7.0,8.0,9.0,10.0,11.0,12.0,13.0,1